<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN GOVT OWNED 616 MLN RAND IN HOUSING BONDS.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN GOVT OWNED 616 MLN RAND IN HOUSING BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close to 40,000 home-owners owed the South African government 616 million rand in arrear bond (mortgage) payments, Housing Minister Sankie Mthembi-Mahanyele told parliament on Wednesday.</p>
<p>She said in a written response to a question that the backlog applied only to state-owned houses.</p>
<p>She said no debts had been written off and no one had yet been evicted.</p>
<p>-- Parliament newsroom +27 21 4032502</p>
